.TH pepe 1  pepe "User Commands"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
pepe \- HTTP load generator
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpepe\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-number\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-concurrency\fR] [\fB\-z\fR|\fB\-\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-curl\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-method\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-headers\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-warmup\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-body\fR] [\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-user\-agent\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-proxy\fR] [\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-insecure\fR] [\fB\-\-disable\-compression\fR] [\fB\-\-disable\-keepalive\fR] [\fB\-\-disable\-redirects\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-trace\-header\fR] [\fB\-\-vars\fR] [\fB\-\-webhook\fR] [\fB\-\-webhook\-on\fR] [\fB\-\-snapshot\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-host\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-requests\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-concurrency\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-if\fR] [\fB\-\-metrics\fR] [\fB\-\-otlp\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-setup\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-write\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-load\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\fR] [\fB\-\-record\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIURL\fR] [\fIARGS\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
HTTP load generator
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-number\fR \fI<NUMBER>\fR [default: 100]
Number of requests to perform
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-concurrency\fR \fI<CONCURRENCY>\fR [default: one per core]
Number of concurrent requests at a time
.TP
\fB\-z\fR, \fB\-\-duration\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
Duration of the test, e.g. 10s, 3m, 2h (mutually exclusive with \-n)
.TP
\fB\-\-curl\fR
Load\-test a curl command: pepe \-\-curl \-\- curl \-X POST http://localhost:8080, or pass it as one quoted string, as @file, or on stdin
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-method\fR \fI<METHOD>\fR [default: GET]
HTTP method, e.g. GET, POST, PUT, DELETE
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-headers\fR \fI<HEADERS>\fR
HTTP headers, e.g. \-H \*(AqAccept: application/json\*(Aq
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<TIMEOUT>\fR [default: 20]
Time in seconds to wait for a response
.TP
\fB\-\-warmup\fR \fI<TIME>\fR
Send for this long before measuring, e.g. 5s: connections open, caches fill and JITs settle without counting against the run
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N|auto>\fR
Threads sending requests (default 1), or "auto" to add one whenever those sending are all busy. One sends 100k requests a second or more; the dashboard says when it is the limit
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\fR \fI<PER_SECOND>\fR
Start this many requests a second, spread evenly, instead of as many as the concurrency allows; \-c is then the most in flight at once, and pepe says when it holds the rate back
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-body\fR \fI<BODY>\fR
HTTP request body
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-user\-agent\fR \fI<USER_AGENT>\fR
User\-Agent string, default is pepe/{version}
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-proxy\fR \fI<PROXY>\fR
Proxy server URL: http://user:pass@host:port or socks5://host:port
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR
Accept invalid TLS certificates (self\-signed, expired, wrong host)
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-compression\fR
Disable HTTP compression, e.g. gzip
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-keepalive\fR
Disable HTTP keepalive, e.g. Connection: close
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-redirects\fR
Prevent http redirects
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output results in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\-header\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Response header holding the request id to show for the slowest requests and in the inspector, so they can be found in the server\*(Aqs logs; without it, X\-Request\-Id, traceparent, CF\-Ray, X\-Amzn\-Trace\-Id and other common ones are looked for
.TP
\fB\-\-vars\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Fill the {{holes}} in the URL, headers and body from this CSV file, whose first line names them: each request takes the next row, and the rows go round again. In a flow, each chain starts with the next row\*(Aqs values
.TP
\fB\-\-webhook\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Send the run\*(Aqs verdict to this URL when it ends: a Slack, Discord, Teams or Google Chat webhook gets a message laid out for it, anything else the JSON report; repeat for more. ${NAME} is taken from the environment. A [[webhook]] table in pepe.toml says more
.TP
\fB\-\-webhook\-on\fR \fI<EVENTS>\fR
When the \-\-webhook URLs are sent: start, progress, anomaly, end, fail (the end when a \-\-fail\-if was crossed), comma\-separated; end by default
.TP
\fB\-\-snapshot\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the JSON report so far to this file every minute while the run goes, and once more when it ends, so a long run\*(Aqs numbers survive a crash or a lost terminal; it has a minute\-by\-minute timeline of the whole run
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-host\fR \fI<HOST>\fR
Refuse to send anywhere but these hosts: api.example.com exactly, or .example.com for it and its subdomains; repeat for more. Every target is checked before anything is sent
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-requests\fR \fI<N>\fR
Refuse a run that would send more requests than this: \-n above it, or \-z without a \-\-rate that bounds it
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-rate\fR \fI<PER_SECOND>\fR
Refuse a \-\-rate above this, and a run with no \-\-rate at all, which sends as fast as the target answers
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-concurrency\fR \fI<N>\fR
Refuse a concurrency above this
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Say what would be sent, to where and how much, and send nothing; as JSON with \-\-json
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-if\fR \fI<CONDITION>\fR
End with exit code 4 when the run crosses this, for CI and scripts: \*(Aqp99 > 300ms\*(Aq, \*(Aqerrors > 1%\*(Aq; repeat for more. The report is still printed. (pepe ping has \-\-slo for the same.)
.TP
\fB\-\-metrics\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR
Serve the live numbers for Prometheus at http://ADDR/metrics while the run goes, e.g. :9100 or 127.0.0.1:9100, so a soak run or a long ping shows up in Grafana next to the server\*(Aqs own
.TP
\fB\-\-otlp\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR
Take the service\*(Aqs OpenTelemetry spans at ADDR (OTLP over HTTP, as :4318) and say where its time went: each request carries its own traceparent, and the report breaks the server\*(Aqs time down by span. Point the service at it: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-setup\fR
Open the setup screen to review or change the settings before starting (it opens by itself when no URL is given)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read settings from this file instead of ./pepe.toml; flags on the command line win over it
.TP
\fB\-\-write\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the settings as they stand to this file, as a pepe.toml, and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-load\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Run a test saved on the setup screen (ctrl\-s): ./.pepe/tests/NAME.toml; flags on the command line win over it
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\fR [\fI<NAME>\fR]
Keep the settings as they stand as a saved test, ./.pepe/tests/NAME.toml, then run. With \-\-load and no NAME, the loaded test is updated in place; with another NAME, it\*(Aqs copied
.TP
\fB\-\-record\fR
Keep the run\*(Aqs report under its saved test when it ends, as ./.pepe/runs/NAME/<moment>.json; the run has to be a saved test (\-\-load NAME, or \-\-keep NAME)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIURL\fR] [default: ]
HTTP url to request
.TP
[\fIARGS\fR] [default: ]
List of arguments to pass to curl command
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
pepe\-ping(1)
Ping a URL: a request a second, each split into DNS, connect, TLS, first byte and download, on a graph
.TP
pepe\-ramp(1)
Raise the load step by step to find where the target stops keeping up
.TP
pepe\-compare(1)
Hold a run\*(Aqs JSON report against an earlier one and say what moved
.TP
pepe\-rerun(1)
Run a saved test again, record the run, and say what moved since the run before
.TP
pepe\-history(1)
The saved tests and their recorded runs
.TP
pepe\-api(1)
Load\-test every endpoint of an OpenAPI spec
.TP
pepe\-flow(1)
Run a sequence of requests from a flow file, each step fed by the last
.TP
pepe\-replay(1)
Send the URLs of an access log in their real proportions
.TP
pepe\-logs(1)
Read nginx logs: requests per second now, against each minute, hour and day
.TP
pepe\-schema(1)
Print the JSON Schema of a report: run (the default), ramp, ping or compare
.TP
pepe\-mcp(1)
Serve pepe\*(Aqs modes as tools for an agent over stdio (the Model Context Protocol); the guardrail flags given here hold for every call
.TP
pepe\-self\-update(1)
Update pepe to the latest release, or say what\*(Aqs new in it
.TP
pepe\-completions(1)
Tab completion for your shell: print the script, or \-\-install it
.TP
pepe\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "DASHBOARD KEYS"
.TP
\fBspace, p\fR
Pause or resume sending; a timed run\*(Aqs clock stops while paused
.TP
\fB+, \-\fR
Raise or lower concurrency by about 10%, live
.TP
\fBs, i\fR
Stop sending and keep the results on screen
.TP
\fBr\fR
Restart with the same settings (and the current concurrency)
.TP
\fBe\fR
Back to the setup screen (or, in API mode, the plan)
.TP
\fBtab, left, right, 1\-3\fR
Switch view
.TP
\fBup, down, j, k, PgUp, PgDn, home, end\fR
Select a request in the log
.TP
\fBf\fR
Filter requests by status: 2xx, 3xx, 4xx, 5xx, no response, failed
.TP
\fBl\fR
Filter requests by latency: at or above p50, p90 or p99
.TP
\fB/\fR
Search the status and response text
.TP
\fBx\fR
Show only failed requests
.TP
\fBc\fR
Clear all filters
.TP
\fBenter\fR
Inspect the selected request; esc goes back
.TP
\fB?\fR
Show all keys
.TP
\fBq, esc, Ctrl\-C\fR
Quit
.SH "SETUP SCREEN KEYS"
.TP
\fBtab\fR
Switch mode: Single URL, Ramp or API
.TP
\fBup, down\fR
Move between fields; left, right change a choice
.TP
\fBenter\fR
Start the run (or load the spec, in API mode)
.TP
\fBctrl\-t\fR
Send the request once and show the response
.TP
\fBctrl\-s\fR
Save the form as pepe.toml
.TP
\fBF1\fR
Show all keys (? too, outside a text field)
.TP
\fBesc\fR
Quit
.SH "RAMP KEYS"
.TP
\fBup, down\fR
Pick a step and see everything measured about it; esc follows the run again
.TP
\fBspace\fR
Pause or resume; a step\*(Aqs clock stops while paused
.TP
\fBn\fR
End this step now and go on to the next
.TP
\fBs\fR
Stop the ramp here and keep the results
.TP
\fBr, e\fR
Run again; back to the setup screen
.TP
\fB?\fR
Show all keys
.SH "PING KEYS"
.TP
\fBtab, 1\-3\fR
Graph, Phases or Pings
.TP
\fBup, down\fR
Pick a target, or a ping in the list
.TP
\fBspace\fR
Pause or resume the pings
.TP
\fB+, \-, w\fR
Half or twice the time on the graph; the whole run
.TP
\fB0, l, s, f\fR
Start at zero; a log scale; dots instead of braille; hide the failures
.TP
\fBt\fR
The table over the whole run, or over what the graph shows
.TP
\fBa, x\fR
Pings: one target or all; failures only
.TP
\fBenter\fR
Pings: everything about the picked one
.TP
\fB?\fR
Show all keys
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBpepe ping https://example.com api.example.com \-\-slo total=500\fR
A request a second to each, split into DNS, connect, TLS, first byte and download, on a graph
.TP
\fBpepe compare before.json after.json\fR
What moved between two runs, and whether it is more than runs wobble
.TP
\fBpepe logs /var/log/nginx/access.log /var/log/nginx/error.log\fR
Requests per second now, against each minute, hour and day of the log
.TP
\fBpepe replay access.log \-\-base\-url https://staging.example.com \-c 50 \-z 2m\fR
The log\*(Aqs URLs, in their real proportions
.TP
\fBpepe flow checkout.toml \-c 20 \-z 1m\fR
A sequence of requests, each step fed by the one before
.TP
\fBpepe https://example.com\fR
100 requests, one per core at a time, with the dashboard
.TP
\fBpepe \-z 30s \-c 50 https://example.com\fR
Thirty seconds at concurrency 50
.TP
\fBpepe \-\-curl \-\- curl \-X POST https://httpbin.org/post \-d \*(Aq{"a":1}\*(Aq\fR
The request a curl command would send
.TP
\fBpepe ramp https://example.com \-\-to 200 \-\-until \*(Aqp99 > 500ms\*(Aq\fR
Raise the load until p99 passes 500 ms
.TP
\fBpepe \-\-json \-n 1000 https://example.com > results.json\fR
No dashboard; a JSON report
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBPEPE_NO_UPDATE_CHECK\fR
Set to anything to skip the look for a newer release
.TP
\fBPEPE_GITHUB_TOKEN\fR
A GitHub token for pepe self\-update, for forks or rate\-limited CI
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
Set to anything to draw without colour: reverse video and shades instead
.TP
\fBPEPE_THEME\fR
A theme by name (pepe, nord, dracula, gruvbox, tokyo\-night, catppuccin, paper, terminal, light, none); otherwise the one saved in the settings (F2 on any screen), or what the terminal suggests
.TP
\fBPEPE_CONFIG_DIR\fR
Where settings.toml is kept: the theme and this machine\*(Aqs defaults (~/.config/pepe otherwise)
.SH "SEE ALSO"
pepe\-ping(1), pepe\-ramp(1), pepe\-api(1), pepe\-self\-update(1), and \fBhttps://github.com/omarmhaimdat/pepe\fR
